{
    "background_story": "Rodrigo was a renowned paleontologist with a passion for uncovering the secrets of the ancient world. His life's work was dedicated to studying the Trachodon, a mysterious hadrosaurid dinosaur that roamed the earth during the Late Cretaceous period. Rodrigo's fascination with the Trachodon began when he was a young boy, poring over dusty tomes in his local library. Years of tireless research and excavation led him to a groundbreaking discovery: a nearly complete Trachodon skeleton in the badlands of Montana. Rodrigo's findings shed new light on the dinosaur's behavior, habitat, and evolution, earning him international acclaim and a coveted spot in the paleontological hall of fame. His dedication to unraveling the mysteries of the Trachodon inspired a new generation of scientists to follow in his footsteps.",
